# SELinux rules for MiTun.
#
# Mihomo is invoked from KernelSU's `su` domain. On most stock Android builds
# the `su` domain is already permissive enough that these rules are a no-op
# safety net. Keep them as a minimal contract rather than an exhaustive list:
#   - tun_device chr_file I/O: open /dev/net/tun and issue TUNSETIFF ioctls.
#   - capability net_admin / net_raw: manage routes, rules, and raw sockets.
#
# If you hit avc denials in dmesg (`dmesg | grep avc | grep mihomo`), add the
# specific rule rather than broadening these. Do NOT copy unrelated denials
# from other modules — they usually don't apply.

allow su tun_device chr_file { read write ioctl open getattr };
allow su self capability { net_admin net_raw };
